To build one, the following things are needed:
-Lightweight-filament (I did it with ASA Aero)
-Normal PLA/PETG filament
-3d printer capable of printing engineering filaments
-4 micro-servos (mg90s) + Miuzei MS18
-two DX-LR03 Antennas
-two ESP32 S3 CAM
-Heat brass inserts ( 8x M2; 4x M3; 2x M4 )
-Screws corresponding to the brass inserts + 6x screws for 3d prints
-Straight spring steel wire (2,6mm x1m; 1,5mm x10cm)
-24cm Carbon pipe 1cm diameter
-D Power Comet 40A, D Power AL2835-6, Tattu Fun fly 4s 1550mAh
-PCB (Files in 3D-model)
-seven  1x3pin headers, one 1x7 socket strip and two 20x1 socket strips
-two 37mm diameter wheels with 27mm axle bores and one 19mm diameter wheel with 1,6mm axle bore
-3D print glue and hot glue
